We have a project here at Volvo where we are trying to evaluating the
values of DCE as a part of our distributed environment. Inside Volvo 
you can unfortunately find all types of machines today, which isn't going
to make the work easier. But apart from most technical questions there
arises others which is as interesting for not so small companies like Volvo 
who primarily is going to use DCE and maybe not developing so many 
applications of our own.

The RFT way of solving the problem with which technology to choose
is an interesting aproach but what is happening from now on with these
technologies? 

Are the technologies frozen (as Motif??) or are they going to be developed? 

Who is going to develop them further? 

Has the contributing companies in some way promised to share their new 
developments of the DCE technologies with OSF for future incorporation in the 
OSF/DCE?

Can the contributing companies develop and market their own better products
based on these technologies which isn't necessarily compatible with DCE?

Who is responsible for interoperability between two platforms running
OSF/DCE when you have your service agreement with two companies? Who
can decide which company should be responsible for a certain problem?

I have loads of other more fuzzy questions (if possible) but would like
to discuss these first. Any comments and/or answers are welcome!

Yours

        "
