The DCE calls in your code should not require modification.
Nor do you have to expend any effort to accomodate the possibility
that your client is on NT and the server is on SUN OS.
You still have to be careful to write portable code for the
rest of your application.

>	
>2.	I have an application that is currently working fine with 
>HP RPC (Network Computing System).  How easy it is to convert it to
>DCE RPC?  I understand that the DCE comes with a Kerboros security
>system.  Can I easily integrate that kerboros thing into my NCS application?
>Is there any documentation for transition from NCS RPC to DCE RPC?

DCE RPC looks very much like NCS, but there are differences
in both the IDL and in the service subroutines.  The mapping between
them is usually straightforward.  Digital's DCE product includes
a tool to convert from NCS to DCE; I don't know about other
vendors.  A Server converted from NCS to DCE can be configured to
accept requests from both new DCE clients and old NCS  clients.

Kerberos authentication is well integrated into DCE, and an application
can take advantage of with just a few lines of code.

